The code statements that lead to the bug are:
in svc_defer():
    if (test_bit(RQ_USEDEFERRAL, &rqstp->rq_flags))
        set_bit(RQ_DROPME, &rqstp->rq_flags);
in cache_check():
    svc_defer(rqstp);
Reason: During NFSv4 compound argument decoding, an operation such as SETATTR triggers an idmap upcall. When the upcall response is delayed, cache_check() returns -EAGAIN and calls svc_defer(). Because the generic RPC layer sets RQ_USEDEFERRAL, svc_defer() sets RQ_DROPME, causing the request to be dropped before nfs4svc_encode_compoundres() runs. The session slot's NFSD4_SLOT_INUSE flag is then never cleared, making the slot permanently unusable.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
in nfs4svc_decode_compoundargs():
    clear_bit(RQ_USEDEFERRAL, &rqstp->rq_flags);
Reason: Clearing RQ_USEDEFERRAL before any NFSv4 operation decoding prevents svc_defer() from ever setting RQ_DROPME during idmap lookups. This ensures the compound request is not dropped prematurely, so encoding completes normally and the session slot is properly released.

